{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/482765-dark-ages-breaking-points","id":482765,"title":"Dark Ages Breaking Points","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-16T14:11:56-07:00","id":482765,"title":"Dark Ages Breaking Points","content":"Would Breaking Points be different in the Dark Ages (or roman times) or whatever? I think a Medieval Knight would be way more used to killing than a normal person today. Or am I misunderstanding things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T14:31:10-07:00","id":482817,"title":"","content":"The problem, I believe, is that the concept of Breaking Points is rooted in the basic foundation of the human psyche, such that it takes becoming something else to get rid of it. You might, however, handle what you're going for by giving them a blanket bonus of one or two die when rolling for violence induced Breaking Points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T14:34:29-07:00","id":482821,"title":"","content":"It has been said that the focus on killing is mostly on &quot;vampiric&quot; killing, i.e. from feeding or by punching someone so hard his guts fly out the back. Regular killing might still be a Breaking Point, but that is more dependent on the individuall.<br /> <br /> As such, most Breaking Points should be identical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T15:06:04-07:00","id":482838,"title":"","content":"I see no reason for there to be any differences. Maybe for those non-vampiric killings you could boost the level of them as a general rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T17:19:41-07:00","id":482965,"title":"","content":"One has to compare apples to apples. A medieval knight is as used to killing as an infantry-man today is. Even then, most probably haven't killed someone. If you're gonna compare a normal person today, you have to use a normal person then. A medieval peasant is incredibly unlikely to have killed someone, I'd guess, and the trauma of having ended somebodies life with your own hands would be the same even if life was shorter and death a little more prevalent in ever-day life. <br /> <br /> Secondly, as said above, new Humanity breaking points are more about being reminded that you're not human and becoming detached than they are about some sort of debunked pseudo-psycho babble about how being an immoral person makes you get mental diseases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T17:21:54-07:00","id":482966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/482765-dark-ages-breaking-points#post482765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Breaking Points be different in the Dark Ages (or roman times) or whatever? I think a Medieval Knight would be way more used to killing than a normal person today. Or am I misunderstanding things.</div> </div> </div> </div>A character who is &quot;used to&quot; killing is so because she's become desensitized to it, due to having low Integrity/Humanity, and/or eliminating the Breaking Point with a Bane. You might be able to justify starting characters at lower Integrity/Humanity, due to Breaking Points being more commonplace in daily life, I suppose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T20:07:55-07:00","id":483126,"title":"","content":"All good! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T04:37:22-07:00","id":483409,"title":"","content":"Of the sample breaking points the only one I see as maybe different for the Dark Ages would be the family deaths. Specific to that time period, life spans were short and poor medical care meant people died more often than they do today. I might bump the humanity level up for those breaking points. Witnessing death probably wasn't as much a shock in those days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T05:09:43-07:00","id":483428,"title":"","content":"I'm on the always breaking points side of things, but I think you could get modifiers if you had the blessings or forgiveness of the church or it was your job and you were doing it in the course of your job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:29:47-07:00","id":485517,"title":"","content":"&quot;There but for the grace of God [because He allowed me to become an undead monster] I go&quot;.<br /> There were lots of grim ways to die prematurely in the Middle Ages, but vampires wouldn't be susceptible to a lot of them. If a vampire's family dies in a famine or plague, he'll be thinking about how he survived. I expect that banes were more common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}